BT 1 0 0 1 0 74.5 Tm .546625 Tw 14 TL /F1 9.5 Tf .133333 .133333 .133333 rg (India's agricultural landscape is characterized by tremendous regional diversity and seasonal dynamism. Cultivation) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.389962 Tw (cycles are structured around three primary seasons: ) Tj /F2 9.5 Tf (Kharif) Tj /F1 9.5 Tf ( \(monsoon-dependent crops like Rice, Cotton, and) Tj T* 0 Tw .864821 Tw (Maize\), ) Tj /F2 9.5 Tf (Rabi) Tj /F1 9.5 Tf ( \(winter crops like Wheat, Barley, and Mustard\), and ) Tj /F2 9.5 Tf (Summer/Zaid) Tj /F1 9.5 Tf ( \(irrigated short-duration crops like) Tj T* 0 Tw .157031 Tw (pulses and vegetables\), along with perennial whole-year crops such as Coconut and Sugarcane. Over 86% of Indian) Tj T* 0 Tw .4475 Tw (cultivators are smallholder and marginal farmers with landholdings under 2 hectares, making them highly vulnerable) Tj T* 0 Tw (to economic and climatic shocks.) Tj T* ET
